From: SoC Labs soclabs-openocd recipe
Subject: [PATCH] register the hostio4 adapter driver (OpenOCD v0.12.0)

Vendored VERBATIM (below the first blank-line-separated header) from
github.com/SoC-Labs/soclabs-openocd @ 39eba5814063
patches/0002-register-hostio4-v0.12.0.patch. It edits configure.ac, so the
package autoreconfs (Buildroot's OPENOCD_AUTORECONF = YES already). The
driver source is 0104-add-hostio4-driver.patch. Provenance + pins: README.md.

# Registration-only: configure.ac + src/jtag/drivers/Makefile.am + src/jtag/interfaces.c.
# The driver .c is NOT here -- it comes in via 'overlay' from the repo that owns
# it, same as every other driver. Split out of the HOSTIO session's combined
# patch, which embedded a modified copy of hostio4.c and so carried a second
# source of truth for it.
hostio4: nanoSoC HOSTIO4/ADP monitor driver, back-ported to OpenOCD v0.12.0

This is the v0.12.0 (tag 9ea7f3d) variant of hostio4-openocd.patch.  Do NOT
apply both: hostio4-openocd.patch targets master (43441cd) and this one
targets the tag the bench runs.  Apply with `git apply` from the top of a
clean v0.12.0 checkout.

BUILT AND PROVEN: configured and compiled at 9ea7f3d, and all six transport
proofs were re-run against the RTL-cited reference monitor
(HAPS-work/fpga/haps-sx/hostio/adpmon.py) through adp-bridge.  No hardware
was involved.

THREE structural differences from the master patch, not one:

  1. struct adapter_driver at 0.12.0 carries `const char * const *transports`
     (src/jtag/interface.h:212), not master's .transport_ids /
     .transport_preferred_id.  Modelled on rshim.c:513 at this tag.
  2. The adapter-driver extern declarations live in src/jtag/interfaces.c at
     0.12.0; src/jtag/interface.h has no such block, so the master patch's
     interface.h hunk has no counterpart here.
  3. configure.ac at 0.12.0 has no DMEM_ADAPTER m4 group and no
     PROCESS_ADAPTERS([...], [true], [unused]) idiom for always-buildable
     adapters.  The integration follows remote_bitbang's per-driver
     AC_ARG_ENABLE / AS_IF / AM_CONDITIONAL pattern instead.

struct dap_ops at 0.12.0 lacks master's .pre_connect_init and spells the
register argument `unsigned` rather than `unsigned int`; the driver sets
neither, and uses designated initialisers, so it needs no change.

The doc/openocd.texi hunk is dropped here: it applies to master with an
offset and carries no build dependency.

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index eee42d4..3cc0280 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -381,6 +381,10 @@ AC_ARG_ENABLE([remote-bitbang],
   AS_HELP_STRING([--enable-remote-bitbang], [Enable building support for the Remote Bitbang jtag driver]),
   [build_remote_bitbang=$enableval], [build_remote_bitbang=no])
 
+AC_ARG_ENABLE([hostio4],
+  AS_HELP_STRING([--disable-hostio4], [Disable building support for the nanoSoC HOSTIO4/ADP monitor driver]),
+  [build_hostio4=$enableval], [build_hostio4=yes])
+
 AS_CASE(["${host_cpu}"],
   [i?86|x86*], [],
   [
@@ -593,6 +597,12 @@ AS_IF([test "x$build_remote_bitbang" = "xyes"], [
   AC_DEFINE([BUILD_REMOTE_BITBANG], [0], [0 if you don't want the Remote Bitbang JTAG driver.])
 ])
 
+AS_IF([test "x$build_hostio4" = "xyes"], [
+  AC_DEFINE([BUILD_HOSTIO4], [1], [1 if you want the nanoSoC HOSTIO4/ADP driver.])
+], [
+  AC_DEFINE([BUILD_HOSTIO4], [0], [0 if you don't want the nanoSoC HOSTIO4/ADP driver.])
+])
+
 AS_IF([test "x$build_sysfsgpio" = "xyes"], [
   build_bitbang=yes
   AC_DEFINE([BUILD_SYSFSGPIO], [1], [1 if you want the SysfsGPIO driver.])
@@ -745,6 +755,7 @@ AM_CONDITIONAL([USB_BLASTER_DRIVER], [test "x$enable_usb_blaster" != "xno" -o "x
 AM_CONDITIONAL([AMTJTAGACCEL], [test "x$build_amtjtagaccel" = "xyes"])
 AM_CONDITIONAL([GW16012], [test "x$build_gw16012" = "xyes"])
 AM_CONDITIONAL([REMOTE_BITBANG], [test "x$build_remote_bitbang" = "xyes"])
+AM_CONDITIONAL([HOSTIO4], [test "x$build_hostio4" = "xyes"])
 AM_CONDITIONAL([BUSPIRATE], [test "x$enable_buspirate" != "xno"])
 AM_CONDITIONAL([SYSFSGPIO], [test "x$build_sysfsgpio" = "xyes"])
 AM_CONDITIONAL([XLNX_PCIE_XVC], [test "x$build_xlnx_pcie_xvc" = "xyes"])
diff --git a/src/jtag/drivers/Makefile.am b/src/jtag/drivers/Makefile.am
index 6410f37..a5a2d47 100644
--- a/src/jtag/drivers/Makefile.am
+++ b/src/jtag/drivers/Makefile.am
@@ -141,6 +141,9 @@ endif
 if REMOTE_BITBANG
 DRIVERFILES += %D%/remote_bitbang.c
 endif
+if HOSTIO4
+DRIVERFILES += %D%/hostio4.c
+endif
 if HLADAPTER_STLINK
 DRIVERFILES += %D%/stlink_usb.c
 endif
diff --git a/src/jtag/interfaces.c b/src/jtag/interfaces.c
index 67bbb3b..e117b8b 100644
--- a/src/jtag/interfaces.c
+++ b/src/jtag/interfaces.c
@@ -100,6 +100,9 @@ extern struct adapter_driver buspirate_adapter_driver;
 #if BUILD_REMOTE_BITBANG == 1
 extern struct adapter_driver remote_bitbang_adapter_driver;
 #endif
+#if BUILD_HOSTIO4 == 1
+extern struct adapter_driver hostio4_adapter_driver;
+#endif
 #if BUILD_HLADAPTER == 1
 extern struct adapter_driver hl_adapter_driver;
 #endif
@@ -220,6 +223,9 @@ struct adapter_driver *adapter_drivers[] = {
 #if BUILD_REMOTE_BITBANG == 1
 		&remote_bitbang_adapter_driver,
 #endif
+#if BUILD_HOSTIO4 == 1
+		&hostio4_adapter_driver,
+#endif
 #if BUILD_HLADAPTER == 1
 		&hl_adapter_driver,
 #endif
